# File-Header Contracts

Every non-trivial `app/**/*.py` file needs a module docstring as the **first statement** with all 7 fields:

```python
# app/path/to/file.py
"""
Bounded Context:  <e.g. BC5 — Execution Runtime>
Responsibility:   <one sentence>
Owns:             <classes/functions defined here>
Public Surface:   <what callers import>
Must NOT:         <hard import/behavior constraints>
Dependencies:     <direct deps>
Reason To Change: <single reason to modify>
"""
from __future__ import annotations  # AFTER docstring
```

Exempt: empty/`#`-only `__init__.py`, tiny `__main__.py`. Logic-bearing `__init__.py` must have a contract.

BC names: BC1 Graph Language, BC2 Node Contract, BC3 Node Catalog, BC4 Execution Planner, BC5 Execution Runtime, BC6 Observability & Storage; plus Domain / API / CLI / MCP labels as in `.kiro/steering/file-header-contracts.md`.

`Must NOT` must name forbidden imports (e.g. no `app.domain` from platform storage).
